.SH NAME
tmh-freeze - Capture live tmux state into config.yml (non-destructive merge)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtmh freeze [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture the live tmux state and merge it into ~/.config/tmh/config.yml,
preserving comments, templates, and profiles. Sessions or windows absent
from the config are added (with an inferred root when possible); existing
entries with matching dirs are left untouched; mismatches are reported as
conflicts — review them and apply with "tmh sync --pull --all" or by hand.

.PP
This is the authoring complement to "tmh diff": build your layout live,
then freeze it into the config so drift detection becomes meaningful.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	report planned changes without writing the file

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for freeze

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	freeze only the named live session


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to config.yml (overrides TMH_CONFIG and defaults)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	language override (en|ru); takes precedence over config and env

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile name from config.yml


